From: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
Subject: [PATCH] TEMPORARY: drm/amd/display: hide GFX6-8 modifiers until Mesa 26.3

Drop this patch once the distribution ships Mesa 26.3.

Since Linux 7.3, DC exposes DRM format modifiers on GFX6-8. Mesa before
26.3 rejects every modifier on GFX6-8, LINEAR included, so allocating
with the plane IN_FORMATS list fails. Mutter allocates the scanout
buffers of a secondary GPU that way without a fallback, so an external
display on the dGPU of a MacBookPro15,1 stays dark.

Expose no modifiers on GFX6-8 again, as before Linux 7.3. DC takes the
tiling only from the modifier, so keep converting the tiling flags of
framebuffers without modifiers and accept the converted modifier in the
plane check.

Signed-off-by: Andre Eikmeyer <dev@deq.rocks>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c             |  3 ++-
 drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c | 18 ++++++++++++++++--
 2 files changed, 18 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c
index 59ea338..0bd2020 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_display.c
@@ -1418,7 +1418,8 @@ static int amdgpu_display_framebuffer_init(struct drm_device *dev,
 			return ret;
 	}
 
-	if (!dev->mode_config.fb_modifiers_not_supported &&
+	/* DC takes the tiling only from the modifier. */
+	if ((!dev->mode_config.fb_modifiers_not_supported || adev->dc_enabled) &&
 	    !(rfb->base.flags & DRM_MODE_FB_MODIFIERS)) {
 		if (amdgpu_ip_version(adev, GC_HWIP, 0) >= IP_VERSION(12, 0, 0))
 			ret = convert_tiling_flags_to_modifier_gfx12(rfb);
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
index a2b8f70..6ab394d 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/display/amdgpu_dm/amdgpu_dm_plane.c
@@ -994,6 +994,16 @@ static void amdgpu_dm_plane_add_gfx12_modifiers(struct amdgpu_device *adev,
 STATIC_IFN_KUNIT int amdgpu_dm_plane_get_plane_modifiers(struct amdgpu_device *adev, unsigned int plane_type, uint64_t **mods)
 {
 	uint64_t size = 0, capacity = 128;
+
+	/*
+	 * TEMPORARY: Mesa before 26.3 cannot allocate with GFX6-8 modifiers,
+	 * so a compositor that allocates with the IN_FORMATS list fails. Keep
+	 * them hidden until the distributions ship Mesa 26.3.
+	 */
+	*mods = NULL;
+	if (adev->family < AMDGPU_FAMILY_AI)
+		return 0;
+
 	*mods = kmalloc_array(capacity, sizeof(uint64_t), GFP_KERNEL);
 
 	if (plane_type == DRM_PLANE_TYPE_CURSOR) {
@@ -1853,12 +1863,16 @@ STATIC_IFN_KUNIT bool amdgpu_dm_plane_format_mod_supported(struct drm_plane *pla
 		return true;
 	}
 
-	/* Check that the modifier is on the list of the plane's supported modifiers. */
+	/*
+	 * Check that the modifier is on the list of the plane's supported
+	 * modifiers. Without exposed modifiers it comes from the tiling flags.
+	 */
 	for (i = 0; i < plane->modifier_count; i++) {
 		if (modifier == plane->modifiers[i])
 			break;
 	}
-	if (i == plane->modifier_count)
+	if (i == plane->modifier_count &&
+	    !plane->dev->mode_config.fb_modifiers_not_supported)
 		return false;
 
 	if (AMD_FMT_MOD_GET(TILE_VERSION, modifier) == AMD_FMT_MOD_TILE_VER_GFX6)
